floor: Peter Jennings)  The site of the bombing in Moscow shown; details recalled of last week's downing of two Russian planes.", "segment_duration": 240, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63070.0", "legacy_segment_id": 764206, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "Zp8A7scp36", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-31", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1680, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 764205, "segment_id": "JOBt9vKq9y", "segment_broadcast_id": "Zp8A7scp36", "segment_title": "Campaign 2004 / Bush vs. Kerry / Terrorism / Republican Convention / Demonstrations / Kerry's Military Record", "segment_description": "(Convention floor: Peter Jennings)  Report introduced. \n (Alleman, Iowa: Terry Moran)  President Bush's clarification of his statement that the war on terrorism cannot be won featured.  [In Nashville, BUSH&nbsp- says in this different kind of war, we are winning & we will win; criticizes Senator John Kerry's position on the war in Iraq.]  Tonight's convention speeches by Governor Arnold Schwarzenegger & First Lady Laura Bush previewed. \n (Convention floor: Peter Jennings)  Today's demonstrations in New York City reviewed; scenes shown from the streets. \n (Convention floor: Jake Tapper)  The attacks on Kerry's military service reviewed.  [Two REPUBLICANS&nbsp- joke about Kerry's Purple Hearts.]  [August 23, BUSH&nbsp- says Kerry served admirably.]  [Political analyst Stuart ROTHENBERG&#134;- says Bush is staying above the fray.]  [Kerry campaign adviser Joe LOCKHART&#134;- notes the Bush family behavior.]  [Earlier, former Senator Bob DOLE; yesterday, former President George BUSH&nbsp- question Kerry's record.]", "seg